4. Handle Cache Updates Across Pods
When you update data that affects cached entries, use @CacheEvict to remove stale data. Because Redis is shared, evicting from one pod makes the data unavailable to all pods immediately:

java
@Service
public class YourService {

    @CacheEvict(value = "ownerCache", key = "#type")
    public void updateOwnerByType(String type, String newOwner) {
        // Update your database here
        // Cache is evicted automatically from Redis
    }

    @CacheEvict(value = "lockerCache", key = "#id")
    public void updateLocker(Locker locker) {
        // Update your database here
        // Cache is evicted automatically from Redis
    }
}
