Performance Characteristics
With This Setup:
L1 (Caffeine): ~50-100ns access time, 10,000 entries maximum per pod

L2 (Redis): ~1-5ms access time, unbounded storage

Cross-pod invalidation: ~5-10ms propagation delay

Cache Strategy Summary:
Read operations: Check L1 → L2 → Database

Write operations: Update database, update L1 & L2, broadcast invalidation

Invalidation from other pods: Only clear L1, L2 remains valid

Stale data protection: Short TTL on L1 (1 minute), longer TTL on L2 (10 minutes)

Tuning for Your Workload
yaml
# application.yml
cache:
  l1:
    maximum-size: 20000  # Adjust based on pod memory
    expire-after-write: 2m
  l2:
    expire-after-write: 15m
  invalidation:
    broadcast-enabled: true
This architecture gives you the best of both worlds: Caffeine's microsecond-level latency for hot data in each pod, combined with Redis's shared cache and automatic cross-pod invalidation.



